# Which country puts the most plastic into the ocean?
subtitle: "Pick the country that puts the most plastic into the ocean, then see why it is a nation of islands and small city rivers, not the biggest user."
tags: ["earth","geography","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Not who you'd guess\" note \"1/3 of it\" card charcoal eyes"
voices: {"a":"gemini:Schedar | an even, thoughtful data-journalist quiz host; calm, natural pace","b":"gemini:Zephyr | a bright co-host with confident wrong hunches; natural, never exaggerated","take":"lines"}

## Which country puts the most plastic into the ocean?
affirm: playful
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: Where does the plastic in our oceans come from?
      authors: Hannah Ritchie (Our World in Data)
      year: 2021
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/ocean-plastics
      finding: the Philippines accounts for 36% of plastic inputs to the ocean, India 13%, China 7%; seven of the top ten emitting rivers are in the Philippines; the Pasig river alone carries 6.4% of global river plastic; it takes the top 1,656 rivers to account for 80%
    - id: chart
      title: Share of global plastic waste emitted to the ocean (2019)
      authors: Our World in Data, from Meijer et al. (2021), Science Advances
      year: 2021
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/grapher/share-of-global-plastic-waste-emitted-to-the-ocean
      finding: Philippines 36.4%, India 12.9%, Malaysia 7.5%, China 7.2%, United States 0.25% (2019)

    icon f_us size 200 set twemoji x 200 y 580 icon_look picture of "flag united states" hidden true
    icon f_cn size 200 set twemoji x 500 y 580 icon_look picture of "flag china" hidden true
    icon f_in size 200 set twemoji x 800 y 580 icon_look picture of "flag india" hidden true
    icon f_my size 200 set twemoji x 330 y 300 icon_look picture of "flag malaysia" hidden true
    icon f_ph size 200 set twemoji x 670 y 300 icon_look picture of "flag philippines" hidden true
    text l_us "<1%" right f_us gap 14 #3d3833 cites ["chart"] font_size 50 hidden true

    card title "Who puts most plastic in the sea?"

A: Which country puts the most plastic into the ocean? Five suspects.
    draw f_us f_cn f_in f_my f_ph parallel true

B: Everyone will say China. I'm going with America: all those takeaway cups.
    highlight f_us

    ask "Tap the country you suspect." choose ["f_us","f_cn","f_in","f_my","f_ph"] answer f_ph store c reveal.text "✓ 36%" reveal.at.x 670 reveal.at.y 420 reveal.size 56
        right: The Philippines: more than a third of all the plastic that reaches the sea.
        wrong: Think less about who uses the most plastic, and more about where a country's rubbish can go.

A: China: about seven percent. India, thirteen. And little Malaysia, seven and a half, ahead of China.
    text l_cn "7%" right f_cn gap 14 #3d3833 cites ["chart"] font_size 50
    text l_in "13%" right f_in gap 14 #3d3833 cites ["chart"] font_size 50
    text l_my "7.5%" right f_my gap 14 #3d3833 cites ["chart"] font_size 50

B: And my America?
    highlight f_us

A: Under one percent. Its rubbish is mostly collected and buried, far from rivers.
    draw l_us

    move f_us scale 0.1 duration 0.8

    move f_cn f_my scale 0.45 duration 0.8

    move f_in scale 0.6 duration 0.8

B: Drawn to scale, that's lopsided. Why the Philippines?
    move f_ph scale 1.4 duration 1.2

## Why the Philippines?
use: world_map
with:
    focus:
      - Philippines
    highlight:
      - Philippines
    markers:
      - {at: [120.97, 14.59], label: Pasig}
      - {at: [121.65, 18.36], label: Cagayan}
      - {at: [123.1, 13.65], label: Bicol}
      - {at: [122.56, 10.7], label: Iloilo}
      - {at: [123.9, 10.3], label: Cebu}
      - {at: [124.65, 8.49], label: Cagayan de Oro}
      - {at: [125.53, 8.95], label: Agusan}
      - {at: [125.62, 7.07], label: Davao}
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: Where does the plastic in our oceans come from?
      authors: Hannah Ritchie (Our World in Data)
      year: 2021
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/ocean-plastics
      finding: the Philippines accounts for 36% of plastic inputs to the ocean, India 13%, China 7%; seven of the top ten emitting rivers are in the Philippines; the Pasig river alone carries 6.4% of global river plastic; it takes the top 1,656 rivers to account for 80%

    card title "Why the Philippines?"

    hide marker_0 marker_1 marker_2 marker_3 marker_4 marker_5 marker_6 marker_7 marker_label_0 marker_label_1 marker_label_2 marker_label_3 marker_label_4 marker_label_5 marker_label_6 marker_label_7

A: Thousands of islands, people living near the coast, heavy rain, and rubbish that is often never collected. It's a short trip to the sea.
    draw country_philippines hl_philippines

B: So it's not one giant river, but lots of little ones?
    shape r1 #2f6b8f at.ref marker_1 shape circle radius 7 style.fill #2f6b8f
    shape r2 #2f6b8f at.ref marker_2 shape circle radius 7 style.fill #2f6b8f
    shape r3 #2f6b8f at.ref marker_3 shape circle radius 7 style.fill #2f6b8f
    shape r4 #2f6b8f at.ref marker_4 shape circle radius 7 style.fill #2f6b8f
    shape r5 #2f6b8f at.ref marker_5 shape circle radius 7 style.fill #2f6b8f
    shape r6 #2f6b8f at.ref marker_6 shape circle radius 7 style.fill #2f6b8f
    shape r7 #2f6b8f at.ref marker_7 shape circle radius 7 style.fill #2f6b8f
    parallel true

A: Yes. The Pasig, a small river through Manila, carries six percent of all river plastic by itself.
    shape city #b5482e at.ref marker_0 shape circle radius 9 style.fill #b5482e
    text pasig "Pasig: 6%" #2f6b8f cites ["owid"] x 200 y 520 font_size 48
    arrow p_ar #2f6b8f from.x 290 from.y 505 to.ref city

A: It takes over a thousand rivers to make up most of the world's total. So the fix is collecting rubbish everywhere before it reaches the water.
    text rivers "1,000+ rivers" #2f6b8f cites ["owid"] x 820 y 420 font_size 50

